function help(){if(!appReady)return;showModal(`<div class="eyebrow">FINDR / ${APP_VERSION}</div><h2>Take FINDR on site.</h2><h3>Install on iPhone</h3><ol class="install-steps"><li>Open this site in Safari.</li><li>Tap Share → Add to Home Screen.</li><li>Open FINDR once online. Wait for “App ready offline”.</li><li>Save your panel or device pack. Check its saved count, then try it in airplane mode.</li></ol><h3>Keypad emulator and updates</h3><p style="margin-top:12px">Open Keypads to use the free-use emulator. The guided lessons and documented Menu maps remain available. ${native?'For a newer Android build, install the latest APK as an update to this app.':'Use the release page to check for an app update.'}</p><div class="inline-actions">${action('navigate','Open keypads','secondary','data-value="#emulator"')} ${action('navigate','Menu maps','secondary','data-value="#menus"')}<a class="secondary" href="${RELEASE_URL}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open release page ↗</a></div><h3>What works offline?</h3><p style="margin-top:12px">Panel Pals marked “Ready offline” can use their saved manuals and shared local model. Saved conversations, imported panel schedules, manual search, keypad emulators, menu maps and the field kit also work with their required assets saved. Manual search remains available when local AI cannot run. Online AI and new downloads need a connection.</p><h3>What this build knows</h3><p style="margin-top:12px">${panels.length} pictured panel families, ${packs.length} panel packs, ${devices.length} pictured device families in ${devicePacks.length} device packs, and 58 generic visit routes across fire, access, CCTV, intruder and shared power/cabling. The earlier ${knowledge.groups.length} panel-led guides, including warden call, remain available. Answer Yes, No or I don’t know. Rankings suggest possibilities to investigate; they do not confirm a repair diagnosis. Online AI is optional: only an explicitly enabled conversation sends its question, relevant context and selected manual excerpts through FINDR to the provider you chose (Groq or OpenAI). Online replies require a connection.</p><p>Browser data can be removed by iOS or by clearing website storage. Keep original files and check your offline kit before a call-out.</p><div class="inline-actions">${action('storage','Check device storage','secondary')}<a class="secondary" href="https://github.com/william2535/MANUALARCHIVES" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Manual Archives ↗</a></div><details class="license" style="margin-top:20px"><summary>Credits and method</summary>Each panel and device includes a credit and source link. Manufacturer photos and manual illustrations retain their original ownership. PDFs remain with their publishers. PDF.js (Apache-2.0) is bundled locally. Panel Pals uses the selected offline model or explicitly enabled online AI to interpret requests and select saved manual evidence. Online AI uses your selected provider’s API key for the current browser session; it is not saved in pals or backups. OpenAI API charges are separate from ChatGPT subscriptions. Technical wording is kept to verified PDF extracts and sourced procedures. Earlier guided visits used an information-gain question selector inspired by Akinator’s question-and-database approach. See <a href="https://elokence.com/content/akinator-the-genie" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Elokence</a>.</details>`)}
async function storage(){const estimate=await navigator.storage?.estimate?.();const persistent=await navigator.storage?.persisted?.();showModal(`<h2>On this device</h2><p><strong>${saved.size} PDFs</strong> · ${bytes([...saved.values()].reduce((s,x)=>s+x.bytes,0)).replace('Size unknown','0 MB')}</p><p>App files ${native?'are bundled with the APK':offlineReady?'have been cached for offline use':'are still being prepared'}. ${estimate?'Browser usage: '+bytes(estimate.usage)+' of '+bytes(estimate.quota)+'.':''}</p><p>${persistent?'Persistent storage is enabled.':'Storage persistence is controlled by your browser. Keep original PDFs and verify in airplane mode.'}</p><div class="inline-actions">${action('persist-storage','Request persistent storage','primary')}${action('import','Import a PDF','secondary')}</div>`)}
